From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:06:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 007/160] hjviewer: harden pinned builds against heartbeat
 replies, token leaks and renamed executables
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Heartbeat replies lose `strategy` and `disconnect`: either key lets
  whoever answers /api/heartbeat rewrite options of every PC or end its
  sessions. The hjviewer server answers it with 404, so such a reply
  could only come from a TLS interceptor that the TLS fallback let
  through.
- The account token stays out of PunchHoleRequest and RequestRelay:
  hbbs passes RequestRelay on to the peer unchanged, so the token would
  reach every PC its owner connects to through the relay, and the
  hjviewer server never reads it.
- Windows: settings in the executable name ("…host=…,key=…") no longer
  override the pinned servers and key.
- The note asked for when a session ends is off: it goes to an audit
  API the server does not have.

Each is a thin hook into a function in src/hjviewer.rs; builds without
HJV_SERVER keep upstream's behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
